    skos:definition "Beechnuts are the small, triangular nuts produced by beech trees (genus Fagus), particularly the American beech (Fagus grandifolia) and European beech (Fagus sylvatica). They're edible for humans in moderate amounts, but raw beechnuts contain a compound called fagin (sometimes also referenced as related tannins) that can cause mild digestive upset or headaches if eaten in large quantities. Roasting them reduces this and improves flavor."@en ;
