food_ingredients:bluefish a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:fish ;
    skos:definition "Bluefish (Pomatomus saltatrix) is a species of saltwater fish commonly eaten as food, especially along the Atlantic coasts of the US, and also found in various other parts of the world. Flavor and texture: It has a stronger, more \"fishy\" flavor than mild white fish like cod or tilapia. The flesh is oily/fatty (similar in that regard to mackerel or salmon), which gives it a rich taste but also means it spoils faster and is best cooked fresh."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
