food_ingredients:breadnut-tree-seeds a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:seed ;
    skos:definition "Breadnut (also called kamansi in the Philippines, or \"chataigne\" in the Caribbean) produces large, spiky green fruits similar in appearance to breadfruit, but unlike the common seedless breadfruit variety, breadnut fruits are packed with edible seeds — usually 100+ per fruit. The seeds themselves are roughly the size of chestnuts or large beans. Typically boiled, roasted, or steamed before eating. After cooking, the texture is starchy and nutty, often compared to chestnuts or roasted potatoes."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "breadnut tree seeds"@en ;
