    skos:broader food_ingredients:vegetable ;
    skos:definition "Broccoli raab (also spelled rabe, and sometimes called rapini) is a leafy green vegetable popular in Italian and Mediterranean cooking. Despite its name, it's not closely related to regular broccoli — it's actually more closely related to turnips. It has long, thin stalks with dark green, slightly jagged leaves and small florets that resemble tiny broccoli heads. The whole plant is edible — leaves, stems, and florets. Its defining characteristic is a pleasantly bitter, slightly pungent, nutty flavor, much more assertive than regular broccoli."@en ;
