food_ingredients:chicory-greens a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:leaf-vegetable ;
    skos:definition "Chicory greens are the leafy tops (and sometimes tender inner leaves) of the chicory plant (Cichorium intybus), a bitter leafy vegetable in the same family as endive and radicchio. They're used in cooking much like other bitter greens — think dandelion greens or escarole. Distinctly bitter, with a slight earthiness. The bitterness mellows a lot when cooked."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
