    skos:definition "Cisco is a freshwater whitefish in the genus Coregonus, found mainly in the Great Lakes and other cold lakes across North America (and some in Europe/Asia too). It's related to salmon and trout. Cisco  has a mild, delicate flavor — similar to other whitefish, slightly sweet. The texture is tender, flaky, fine-textured flesh — fairly delicate, can fall apart easily if overcooked."@en ;
