    skos:definition "Enoki mushrooms (also called enokitake, golden needle mushrooms, or velvet shank) are a type of edible mushroom (Flammulina velutipes or filiformis) commonly used in East Asian cuisine, especially Japanese, Korean, and Chinese cooking. Mild, slightly sweet, and faintly fruity flavor; crisp, crunchy texture, even after cooking; Often described as having a delicate, almost noodle-like quality"@en ;
