food_ingredients:eppaw a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:tuber ;
    skos:definition "Eppaw is the edible tuber of the duck potato plant (Sagittaria latifolia, also called wapato or arrowhead), traditionally eaten by some Native American groups, particularly noted in Seminole/Florida contexts. It's a starchy, potato-like root vegetable that grows in shallow water and marshes, and was historically gathered as a wild food source."@en ;
