food_ingredients:feijoa a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:fruit ;
    skos:definition "Feijoa (Acca sellowiana) is a fruit native to South America — specifically the highlands of southern Brazil, Uruguay, Paraguay, and northern Argentina. The flavour is distinctive and hard to compare — often described as a mix of pineapple, guava, mint, and strawberry, with floral notes. The flesh inside is creamy white and slightly gritty near the center, similar to a ripe pear."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "feijoa"@en ;
