    skos:broader food_ingredients:leaf-vegetable ;
    skos:definition "\"Garland chrysanthemum\" (also called tong ho in Chinese, shungiku in Japanese, and ssukgat in Korean) is an edible leafy green — not the ornamental flower you'd put in a bouquet, but a related plant (Glebionis coronaria) grown specifically for eating. Slightly bitter, herbal, and a little peppery — some describe it as tasting faintly like chrysanthemum tea smells."@en ;
