    skos:definition "Irish moss (Chondrus crispus), also called sea moss, is a red seaweed that grows along rocky Atlantic coastlines, especially around Ireland and the Caribbean. In food, it's valued mainly for the natural gelling and thickening properties it gets from carrageenan, a compound extracted from its cell walls. It has a mild, slightly salty or neutral taste on its own, so it's usually blended into other foods rather than eaten plain."@en ;
