food_ingredients:kanpyo a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:altLabel "dried gourd strips"@en ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:vegetable ;
    skos:definition "Kanpyo is a Japanese ingredient made from dried strips of gourd — specifically the flesh of the calabash or bottle gourd (a variety called yūgao, related to what's sometimes called \"bottle gourd\" or \"calabash\" in English). To make it, the gourd is peeled into long, thin ribbons, then sun-dried until they become firm, chewy strips. Before use, the dried strips are rehydrated and usually simmered in a mixture of soy sauce, sugar, and mirin (or dashi) until they turn a light brown color and take on a sweet-savory flavor."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "kanpyo"@en ;
    off:comment "Is this a compound ingredient?"@en ;
    off:usdaNdbCode "11237"@en ;
    off:usdaNdbName "Kanpyo, (dried gourd strips)"@en .

