food_ingredients:leafy-tips-cowpeas a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:leaf-vegetable ;
    skos:definition "Cowpea leafy tips (sometimes called cowpea leaves, or by local names like \"kunde\" in Swahili, \"ewedu\" relatives, or \"bean leaves\") are the young, tender shoot tips and leaves of the cowpea plant (Vigna unguiculata) — the same plant that produces black-eyed peas. While most people know cowpeas for their beans, the leaves are widely eaten as a leafy green vegetable in parts of Africa (especially West and East Africa), as well as in South and Southeast Asia. Slightly bitter, earthy, spinach-like flavor, a bit more robust than spinach."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "leafy tips cowpeas"@en ;
    off:usdaNdbCode "11201"@en ;
    off:usdaNdbName "Cowpeas, leafy tips, raw"@en .

