    skos:altLabel "mahimahi"@en ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:saltwater-fish ;
    skos:definition "Mahi-mahi is a species of fish, it's sometimes called \"dolphinfish,\" but it's unrelated to dolphins. It's a large, colorful saltwater fish found in warm and temperate waters around the world, known for its firm, lean, mildly sweet white-to-pinkish flesh. Flavor and texture: Mild, slightly sweet flavor with a firm, meaty texture — often compared to swordfish or tuna, but lighter and less oily."@en ;
