    skos:broader food_ingredients:cabbage ;
    skos:definition "Mustard Cabbage (also called gai choy or Chinese mustard) is a leafy green vegetable common in Asian cuisine. Large, crinkled or smooth leaves, often with a pale green or yellowish color; can look somewhat like bok choy or napa cabbage. Distinctly pungent and slightly bitter, with a mustardy kick that mellows when cooked."@en ;
