    skos:altLabel "komatsuna"@en ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:leaf-vegetable ;
    skos:definition "Mustard spinach, also known as komatsuna, is a leafy green vegetable that's actually part of the mustard/brassica family (Brassica rapa var. perviridis) rather than being related to true spinach. It's an East Asian vegetable, especially popular in Japanese cuisine (where it's called komatsuna), though it's also grown and eaten in China and other parts of Asia. The flavor is mild and slightly peppery."@en ;
