    skos:altLabel "lulo"@en ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:fruit ;
    skos:definition "Naranjilla is a tropical fruit native to South America, mainly grown in Ecuador, Colombia, and Peru. Small to medium round fruit, about the size of a golf ball with bright orange skin covered in fine, removable fuzz. The flavor is very distinctive — a unique mix of tart, citrusy, and tropical, often described as a cross between pineapple, lime, and rhubarb."@en ;
