    skos:broader food_ingredients:chili-pepper ;
    skos:definition "A Mexican chili. The fresh version of this pepper is actually called chilaca. Once dried, it becomes \"pasilla\" — long, slender, and dark brownish-black with a raisin-like, wrinkled texture. Rich, deep, and slightly fruity with notes of raisin, dried cherry, and mild chocolate/tobacco undertones — a favorite for building complex sauces."@en ;
