food_ingredients:pilinut a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:nut ;
    skos:definition "A pili nut (Canarium ovatum) is a tropical tree nut native to the Philippines, particularly grown in the Bicol region. The nut has a rich, buttery flavor and texture, often compared to a cross between an almond and a macadamia nut — but generally considered even richer and more delicate. They're eaten raw, roasted, or candied, and are also used in pastries, pesto-style sauces, and as a snack food. In the Philippines they're a popular treat, especially when sugar-coated."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "pilinut"@en ;
