    skos:broader food_ingredients:cheese ;
    skos:definition "ROQUEFORT is a sheep milk cheese from the south of France. The cheese is white, tangy, crumbly and slightly moist, with distinctive veins of blue mold. EU law dictates that only those cheeses aged in the natural Combalou caves of Roquefort-sur-Soulzon may bear the name Roquefort, as it is a recognised geographical indication, or has a protected designation of origin."@en ;
