food_ingredients:rose-apple a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:fruit ;
    skos:definition "A rose apple (Syzygium jambos or related species) is a tropical fruit native to Southeast Asia and the Indian subcontinent. Despite its name, it's not related to either roses or apples — it belongs to the myrtle family. Pear- or bell-shaped fruit, usually pale yellow, white, pink, or red, with a waxy, smooth skin. Mildly sweet with a subtle floral aroma reminiscent of roses."@en ;
