food_ingredients:sheepshead a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:saltwater-fish ;
    skos:definition "Sheepshead is the common name for a few different fish species, most notably: (Archosargus probatocephalus), found along the Atlantic and Gulf coasts of North America. Taste and texture: Mild, sweet, and slightly nutty flavor; Firm, white, flaky flesh; Often compared to red snapper, black drum, or grouper; Because it eats mostly shellfish, crabs, and barnacles, some people say the diet gives it a faintly sweet, \"crab-like\" undertone"@en ;
