    skos:broader food_ingredients:fruit ;
    skos:definition "Soursop is a tropical fruit from the Annona muricata tree, native to the Caribbean, Central America, and parts of South America and Africa. Large, green, spiky/prickly on the outside — it can weigh anywhere from 1 to 7 kg. The inside is white, creamy, and fibrous with large black seeds. It's taste is an unique blend of sweet and tangy — often described as a mix of strawberry, pineapple, and citrus, with a creamy texture somewhat like banana or coconut."@en ;
