    skos:definition "Turnip rape (Brassica rapa subsp. oleifera, also called field mustard or rybs in some regions) is grown for its seeds, which are pressed for oil. It's one of the plants used to produce canola oil (along with rapeseed, Brassica napus). Young leaves of turnip rape can be eaten as leafy greens, similar to mustard greens or other brassica greens, in some regional cuisines."@en ;
