food_ingredients:yardlong-beans a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:legume ;
    skos:definition "Yardlong beans (also called Chinese long beans, snake beans, or asparagus beans) are a type of legume known for their dramatically long, slender pods — typically 12 to 30 inches long, though they're usually picked and sold around 18 inches. They have a slightly nuttier, more savory flavor than regular green beans, with a denser, chewier texture that holds up well to high-heat cooking like stir-frying. They're a staple in Chinese, Southeast Asian (especially Thai, Vietnamese, Filipino), and South Asian cooking."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "yardlong beans"@en ;
    off:usdaNdbCode "16133"@en ;
    off:usdaNdbName "Yardlong beans, mature seeds, raw"@en ;
    off:usdaNdbProcess "en:dried"@en .

