food_ingredients:european-perch a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:perch ;
    skos:definition "Der Flussbarsch (Perca fluviatilis), am Bodensee Kretzer, in der Schweiz auch Egli genannt, ist ein in ganz Europa vorkommender Süßwasserfisch."@de,
        "The European perch (Perca fluviatilis), also known as the common perch, redfin perch, big-scaled redfin, English perch, Eurasian perch, Eurasian river perch, Hatch or in Anglophone parts of Europe, simply the perch, is a predatory species of the freshwater perch native to Europe and northern Asia."@en,
        "La perca o perca de río (Perca fluviatilis) es una especie de pez de la familia Percidae muy abundante en los ríos y lagos de casi toda Europa central y occidental."@es,
        "La perche commune, perche franche ou encore perche française en France (Perca fluviatilis) est une espèce de poissons d'eau douce."@fr,
        "Il pesce persico (Perca fluviatilis), conosciuto comunemente in Italia come persico reale o semplicemente persico, è un pesce di acqua dolce."@it,
        "De baars (Perca fluviatilis) is een vis uit de vissenfamilie echte baarzen, die in de Benelux inheems voorkomt."@nl,
        "A Perca fluviatilis é um peixe da família Percidae. Ocorre em rios da Europa e da Ásia."@pt ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "костур"@bg,
        "perca de riu"@ca,
        "okoun říční"@cs,
        "Aborre"@da,
        "Flussbarsch"@de,
        "Πέρκα"@el,
        "European perch"@en,
        "perca europea"@es,
        "ahven"@et,
        "ahven"@fi,
        "perche commune"@fr,
        "Peirse"@ga,
        "grgeč"@hr,
        "Csapósügér"@hu,
        "Pesce persico"@it,
        "Perca fluviatilis"@la,
        "Ešerys"@lt,
        "Asaris"@lv,
        "Åbor"@nn,
        "Okoń europejski"@pl,
        "biban european"@ro,
        "Речной окунь"@ru,
        "Ostriež zelenkastý"@sk,
        "Perca fluviatilis"@sl,
        "Abborre"@sv ;
    off:wikidata wd:Q166812 ;
    off:wikipedia "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_perch"@en .

