    skos:broader food_ingredients:legume,
        food_ingredients:pulse ;
    skos:definition "Hyacinth beans (Lablab purpureus, also called lablab beans, dolichos beans, or Egyptian beans) are a fast-growing climbing vine grown both as an ornamental plant and a food crop. The young, immature pods can be cooked and eaten like green beans. However, the mature beans and pods contain cyanogenic glycosides and must be thoroughly cooked (usually boiled with water changes) before eating — they're toxic raw or undercooked. In parts of Africa and Asia, they're a significant food crop and protein source when properly prepared."@en ;
