    skos:broader food_ingredients:enzyme ;
    skos:definition "LACTASE is essential to the complete digestion of whole milk; it breaks down lactose, a sugar which gives milk its sweetness. Lactase is an enzyme that some people are unable to produce in their small intestine.[5] Without it they can't break down the natural lactose in milk. Lactase produced commercially can be extracted both from yeasts such as Kluyveromyces fragilis and Kluyveromyces lactis and from molds, such as Aspergillus niger and Aspergillus oryzae."@en ;
