food_ingredients:butterfish a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:fish ;
    skos:definition "Butterfish is the common name for a couple of different fish species, most notably: Escolar (Lepidocybium flavobrunneum) — sometimes marketed as \"butterfish,\" this deep-sea fish has an extremely high oil content that gives it a rich, buttery texture and mouthfeel, hence the name. It's popular in sushi restaurants (sometimes mislabeled as \"white tuna\"); American butterfish (Peprilus triacanthus) — a smaller, silvery fish found along the U.S. Atlantic coast."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "butterfish"@en .

