    skos:definition "HORSERADISH (Armoracia rusticana, syn. Cochlearia armoracia) is a perennial plant of the family Brassicaceae. The intact horseradish root has hardly any aroma. When cut or grated enzymes from the now-broken plant cells break down sinigrin (a glucosinolate) to produce allyl isothiocyanate (mustard oil), which irritates the mucous membranes of the sinuses and eyes. Grated mash should be used immediately or preserved in vinegar for best flavor."@en ;
