    skos:definition "A sweet potato is a starchy root vegetable. It grows underground as a swollen root, It's skin can be orange, purple, white, or reddish; flesh is often orange, but also comes in white or purple. It has a naturally sweet flavor, especially when roasted or baked. It is rich in beta-carotene (converts to vitamin A) and a good source of fiber, vitamin C, potassium, and manganese, and has complex carbohydrates, so it digests more slowly than many other starches"@en ;
