        "mais doux"@fr,
        "スィートコーン"@ja,
        "zoete maïs"@nl,
        "słodka kukurydza"@pl ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:corn,
        food_ingredients:pod-and-seed-vegetable ;
    skos:definition "Sweet corn is a cultivar of maize (Zea mays var. saccharata) bred to accumulate higher natural sugar content, harvested young and tender before the kernels mature and starch fully develops. Compared to local field maize, it has a distinctly sweeter, juicier taste with a crisp, tender bite. Popular worldwide, sweet corn is boiled or steamed on the cob, grilled, or used kernel-off-cob in salads, soups, stir-fries, and Indian street snacks like corn chaat. Nutritionally, it offers dietary fiber, carbohydrates, and moderate protein, along with vitamin C, B vitamins (especially folate), magnesium, and antioxidants such as lutein and zeaxanthin, which support eye health. Its natural sweetness also makes it a favorite in both savory and lightly sweetened preparations."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "сладка царевица"@bg,
        "Süßmais"@de,
