food_ingredients:kelp a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:seaweed ;
    skos:definition "Kelp is a type of large brown seaweed that grows in cold, nutrient-rich coastal waters, and it's become a fairly common food ingredient, especially in East Asian cuisines. Kelp is notably rich in iodine, along with other minerals like calcium, magnesium, and iron. It's low in calories and contains some fiber. It has a natural savory, oceanic taste often described as umami. Kelp is a common term covering many species across several genera, all in the order Laminariales."@en ;
