    skos:definition "Mackerel is an oily fish, popular in cuisines around the world for its rich flavor and nutritional value. It is a general name for several related species of fast-swimming, saltwater fish (like Atlantic mackerel, king mackerel, and Spanish mackerel). It has a distinctive striped or mottled pattern on its back and a firm, dark flesh. Taste and texture: Strong, savory, somewhat \"fishy\" flavor compared to milder white fish. The flesh is soft and flaky when cooked, with a high fat content that keeps it moist."@en ;
