    skos:definition "Tilapia is one of the most widely farmed and eaten fish in the world — a mild, freshwater (or brackish-water) fish that's become a staple in supermarkets and restaurants globally. Flavor and texture: Mild, slightly sweet taste with no strong \"fishy\" flavor; Firm, flaky white flesh; Because it's so neutral-tasting, it takes on seasonings, marinades, and sauces well — which is a big part of its popularity"@en ;
