food_ingredients:carp a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:freshwater-fish ;
    skos:definition "Carp is a freshwater fish that's been eaten by humans for thousands of years — it's actually one of the oldest farmed food fish in the world, with cultivation going back to ancient China. Taste and texture: Mild, slightly sweet, and somewhat earthy or \"muddy\" tasting, especially if it comes from murky water. Farm-raised carp raised in cleaner water tends to taste better. The flesh is firm but has a lot of small bones, similar to other freshwater fish like pike."@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "Karpfen"@de,
