    off:comment "Beware of a confusion between the generic name (rapeseed oil) and more specific oil varieties: colza oil and canola oil. Not all languages distinguish between the two. Probably where rapeseed is given, colza is meant. The difference between the two oils is important due to different levels of erucic acid. It seems that only the oils with a low erucic acid percentage are fit for humans. So the naming difference between rapeseed, colza and canola might just be a language issue."@en ;
