food_ingredients:lamb a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:sheep ;
    skos:definition "LAMB, hogget and mutton are the meat of domestic sheep (species Ovis aries) at different ages. The meat of a lamb is taken from the animal between one month and one year old, with a carcase (carcass in American English) weight of between 5.5 and 30 kg. This meat generally is more tender than that from older sheep and appears more often on tables in some Western countries."@en ;
