food_ingredients:pulse a off:FoodIngredient ;
    skos:altLabel "pulses"@en,
        "légume sec"@fr,
        "légumes secs"@fr,
        "légumineuses sèches"@fr ;
    skos:broader food_ingredients:legume ;
    skos:definition "pulse = just the dry, harvested seed of specific legume crops. The UN Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) recognizes 11 categories of pulses: Dry beans — includes kidney beans, navy beans, pinto beans, black beans, lima beans, mung beans, adzuki beans; Dry broad beans — fava beans, horse beans, broad beans (in dried form); Dry peas — includes split peas, whole dried peas (green or yellow); Chickpeas — also called garbanzo beans; Dry cowpeas — black-eyed peas, blackeye beans; Pigeon peas — also called Congo beans or gandules; Lentils — includes red, green, brown, black (beluga), French (Puy); Bambara beans — also called Bambara groundnuts (earth peas); Vetches — common vetch; Lupins — lupin beans (also called lupini beans); Minor pulses — a catch-all for less common ones, such as lablab, jack beans, winged beans, yam beans"@en ;
    skos:inScheme off:food_ingredients ;
    skos:prefLabel "pulse"@en,
        "légumineuse sèche"@fr,
        "puls"@hr,
        "legumi secchi"@it,
        "žāvēti pākšaugi"@lv,
        "gedroogde peulvruchten"@nl,
        "pulso"@pt,
        "baljfrukt"@sv ;
    off:comment "\"en:pulse\" e \"en:legumes\" in italiano spesso si confondono perché entrambi i termini vengono generalmente tradotti come \"legumi\", anche se tecnicamente sarebbe più preciso distinguere tra \"legumi secchi\" (pulses) e \"leguminose\" (legume plants)."@it ;
    off:eurocode2Group2 "7.10"@en ;
    off:wikidata wd:Q2727662 .

